# BabyBlocks-Platform CRM endpoints.
#
# BabyBlocks has its own dedicated CRM stack — the bb-ticket-service
# Cloudflare Worker behind api.babyblocks.io. The marketing-site forms
# (waitlist + newsletter) post directly to that service. Do NOT route
# them to FoundryDesk (studio.foundry-os.io / crm.intriguemmc.com);
# that CRM is for the other brands (IntrigueMMC, IntriguingInsight,
# Foundry, ScreenForge).
#
# Both endpoints are public — no auth header, no bearer token. The
# server applies IP-based rate limiting (5/min) and a CORS allowlist.
# Override either URL at build time for staging by setting the env var.

# Newsletter form — body: { email, name?, list? }
PUBLIC_CRM_LEAD_URL="https://api.babyblocks.io/api/public/newsletter"

# Waitlist form — body: { email, name, app }
#   app ∈ { 'budgetbaby', 'pantrybaby', 'babyblocks-core' }
PUBLIC_WAITLIST_URL="https://api.babyblocks.io/api/public/waitlist"

# Data-request (GDPR/CCPA) form on /data-request.
#
# REQUIRED whenever src/pages/data-request.astro still ships a submitting form —
# `npm run build` fails without it (scripts/assert-dsr-config.mjs). This is the
# variable whose absence let the live form tell customers "Thanks. We got it"
# while recording their statutory request nowhere.
#
# Value is the CRM ORIGIN ONLY — no path, no trailing slash. The page appends
# /api/compliance/babyblocks/dsr-submit itself.
#
# MUST be set in Cloudflare Pages → this project → Settings → Environment
# variables, in BOTH the Production and Preview environments, then redeployed.
# Setting it in Preview only leaves production broken and silent.
#
# KNOWN GAP (verified 2026-09-02): the backend route
# https://api.babyblocks.io/api/compliance/babyblocks/dsr-submit returns 404 —
# it has not been built. With this variable set, the form reports an honest
# failure and points at support@babyblocks.io. Online DSR does not work until
# that route exists.
PUBLIC_CRM_BASE_URL="https://api.babyblocks.io"
